{=1}Amicide

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:23.460
{=2}Best Friend Killer

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:22.750
{=1}Amicide

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:22.910
{=1}Amicide

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:22.960
{=1}Amicide

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:23.080
{=1}Amicide

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:23.460
{=1}Amicide

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:25.460
What?

00:01:57.590 --> 00:02:01.010
Living in a Dead Game

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:03.100
Best Friend Killer?

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:05.560
And what do you mean, "game over"?

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:08.320
To kill your best friend
right off the bat...

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:10.690
you're one messed up
high schooler, huh?

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:11.940
You've got it all wrong!

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:14.450
It was, um, uh...

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:15.450
...an accident!

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:17.620
That's what most murderers say.

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:18.780
It was!

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:22.160
I just gave a little push and
suddenly it was like, splooch!

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:23.290
So it was...

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:24.500
...intentional.

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:25.710
Absolutely not!

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:27.540
Look, just tell me how to reset the game!

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:29.000
You can't, dude.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.880
There are no do-overs in this game.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:35.010
Real life doesn't have a
"New Game" option, right?

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:38.100
That's part of what
it means to pursue realism.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:40.220
What's with the smug look?

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:42.810
Also, <i>Kiwame Quest </i>uses autosave.

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:43.850
Even if you quit right away,

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:46.810
you'd continue from
after killing your best friend.

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:51.900
So then I'm forever stuck with
the title "Best Friend Killer"?

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:54.740
And you can't just buy
another copy of the game.

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:57.160
Your play history is
retained on your hardware.

00:02:57.160 --> 00:03:00.950
To start over you'd have
to purchase a new console.

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:06.000
The VR NX costs 90,000 yen.
At that price, I...

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.790
FYI, I do sell those.

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:10.540
Just 120,000 yen.

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:11.710
That's crazy high!

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:14.840
Enough already! I'm returning this!
Give me my money back!

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:15.840
That's not happening.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:17.220
Wh-Why?

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:18.890
We have a strict policy:

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:23.100
"No refunds, no matter how justified the reason!
(Including damaged or defective goods)"
"--Management"

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:24.180
no refunds---under any circumstances.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:26.520
I'll report you to a consumer agency!

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:29.810
I have no desire to cast a
shadow over your bright future

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:31.150
with a nasty legal battle.

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:33.070
Let's think more constructively.

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:34.610
Constructively?

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:36.650
You said it's already
game over, didn't you?

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:43.080
<i>Kiwame Quest</i>, KQ for short, is a full-dive
RPG sold ten years ago only in Japan.

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:45.410
The company already shut down services.

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:49.920
The player base shrank and shrank,
and it's essentially a dead game.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:54.130
Even so, an extremely small
number of players still remain.

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:56.970
There are people <i>still </i>playing this game?

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.050
It's a big country!

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:02.970
And one of those rare players is Ginji.

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:04.560
Ginji...

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:07.020
Sounds like my money's getting stolen...

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:11.400
Ginji supposedly also killed his best
friend at the start ten years ago.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:13.480
So let's try asking him.

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:15.440
O-Okay.

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:19.150
Oh, but first, check your right pocket.

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:23.580
That's your starting money. Thirty gald.

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:25.240
Let's buy some cheap clothes with it.

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:26.500
Clothes?

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:30.040
I imagine the next stage
of your situation is...

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:32.210
Did you hear about Martin?

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:34.090
Yeah, I heard he was killed.

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:36.630
What?! Who would kill
such a nice young man?

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:40.090
Well... apparently it
was his best friend, Hiro.

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:43.430
The City Guard is looking for him.

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:47.100
There are already wanted posters?

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:51.150
Yup. You're a full-on fugitive.
Get plastic surgery if possible.

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:53.230
Real-life plastic surgery for my avatar?!

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:56.690
Anyway, the clothing store isn't far,
but keep your head down.

00:04:56.690 --> 00:05:00.150
Walk like someone ostracized from society.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:04.580
I don't want to play this game anymore...

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:09.370
This is it, Hiro.

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:12.580
Is it really safe for me to enter a store?

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:15.880
Whether in real life or virtual reality,
stores are all about the customer.

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:19.510
No matter how suspicious you seem,
they won't just immediately report you.

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:21.380
Is that true?

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:24.720
Yes. I should know. I'm a merchant myself!

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:27.180
You're not particularly trustworthy...

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:30.680
Welcome.

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:34.100
Hiro, get this one.

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:38.070
Fifteen gald.

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:40.650
I-I'll take this.

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:42.110
Sure.

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:47.240
Sir, you're the talk
of the town right now.

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:49.660
H-Hey! You said it'd be safe!

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:56.960
Now, now. I'm a businessman.
I'm not reporting my customers.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:58.920
Th-Then...

00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:02.880
Twenty-five gald.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:07.550
He took thorough stock of the situation.
That's KQ's NPCs for you.

00:06:07.550 --> 00:06:08.930
Realistic, right?

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:11.560
I'd call it unpleasant, not realistic!

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:13.850
So I'm also stuck with high prices?

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:17.730
It's yet another reason
we should talk to Ginji.

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:21.400
So, where do we find this Ginji?

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:23.450
Supposedly he's always at the casino.

00:06:23.450 --> 00:06:24.780
Been that way for ten years.

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:27.990
Ten years?! Does he have
a gambling addiction?

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:30.660
Dunno. He's probably just garbage.

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:33.330
That's harsh!

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:39.170
This city's pretty big, huh.

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:43.010
Yes. Though it's inland on
the continent of Alfrey,

00:06:43.010 --> 00:06:46.930
trade with other towns
or castles is prohibited.

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:49.350
It's a massive, self-sufficient city
that's practically closed off.

00:06:49.350 --> 00:06:52.520
The city of Ted, AKA the Closed City.

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:53.890
The Closed City?

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:59.020
FYI, leaving without permission is
punished severely as "exurbance."

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:02.860
No one had a better name for the crime?

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:07.110
Anyway, getting out of the city
is the first step to clearing KQ.

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:09.990
Let's ask Ginji about that, too.

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:17.500
We should be in the clear now.
The casino is close.

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:19.080
Ah, what a relief--

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:21.960
Hiro!

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:33.850
Alicia?!

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:37.980
I found you.

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:40.110
I've looked <i>everywhere</i>.

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:43.400
How? I was even wearing a hood!

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:46.030
I recognized you instantly!

00:07:46.030 --> 00:07:50.410
I've known you since childhood after all.

00:07:52.790 --> 00:07:55.370
What a terrifying childhood friend!

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:58.750
That's the ultra-fast
general-purpose AI R-Evo for you!

00:07:58.750 --> 00:08:01.500
The NPC's have personality,
freedom, and insight--

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:03.710
Be impressed later!

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:06.920
Oh, what's wrong, Hiro?

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:09.680
Why are you talking to yourself?

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:14.430
Oh, right. NPCs can't
perceive Reona's fairy form.

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:17.730
A-Alicia! Hear me out!
It was an accident and...

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:20.440
Yes, I know.

00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:23.610
I went a little crazy there, didn't I?

00:08:23.610 --> 00:08:25.690
So much screaming and shouting...

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:28.820
Oh, but I've calmed down a little now.

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:30.860
Alicia.

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:33.490
I loved you, Hiro.

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:36.370
No, I still love you a ton!

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:37.620
And so I'll...

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:40.170
Th-Thank goodness. Everything's...

00:08:40.170 --> 00:08:41.710
...give you sweet release!

00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:43.880
...not okay at all!

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:47.050
Don't worry. I'll follow soon after.

00:08:47.050 --> 00:08:49.510
The three of us will be friends again

00:08:49.510 --> 00:08:50.800
in the afterlife!

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:52.930
Oh, no! She's totally lost it!

00:08:52.930 --> 00:08:54.760
Come on, Hiro...

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:56.930
Th-That's...

00:08:56.930 --> 00:08:59.100
the knife from...

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:01.900
Yes, I'm Hell's Fruit Slicer--

00:09:01.900 --> 00:09:05.570
The Fruit Knife Wielder From Hell:

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:07.860
Alicia Von Rotarzen!

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:10.990
What kind of title is that? No thank you!

00:09:10.990 --> 00:09:13.320
I'll chop you up into little bits!

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:16.290
Like I'm making apple juice!

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:23.750
Be careful! The childhood
friend's speed is set oddly high.

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:26.630
Lots of players have her join their party.

00:09:26.630 --> 00:09:28.630
She was supposed to join my party?!

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:32.130
It's an open-ended story system,
so it's your choice who joins you.

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:35.390
Though the best friend and
the childhood friend are standard.

00:09:35.390 --> 00:09:38.810
Except I killed one and
the other's about to kill me!

00:09:38.810 --> 00:09:41.890
Hiro, what's all the muttering about?

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:46.860
Oh, of course. You're saying
prayers of repentance!

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:49.320
Hiro!

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:53.570
Hiro! Run! Run! Run!

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:54.910
Don't stop or you're a pincushion!

00:09:54.910 --> 00:09:56.450
Please, no!

00:09:56.450 --> 00:10:00.120
Hiro! Get back here!

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:00.120
T-T-Take a right here!

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:00.870
Okay!

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:01.710
Now a left!

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:02.580
Okay!

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:03.080
Right!

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:04.460
Don't run away!

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:03.620
Okay!

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:04.120
Left!

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:04.460
Okay!

00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:04.920
Right!

00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:05.330
Okay!

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:05.710
Left!

00:10:05.710 --> 00:10:06.130
Okay!

00:10:06.130 --> 00:10:06.500
Right!

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:07.040
Okay!

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:07.540
Left!

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:09.340
Okay!

00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:20.180
Hiro, you're a really fast runner.

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:24.310
The real question is why
I'm so tired in a video game.

00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:29.730
KQ doesn't stop at the five senses.
It reproduces fatigue, too!

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:32.240
I could do without that feature.

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:34.820
Did I level up?

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:39.330
What? "Running Best Friend Killer:
Fleet-footed Amicide"?

00:10:39.330 --> 00:10:42.500
You did it! You got a new title!

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:45.710
Does this raise my speed or something?

00:10:45.710 --> 00:10:48.460
Nope. They're just something you collect!

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:52.300
Let's keep this up and get lots of titles!

00:10:52.300 --> 00:10:55.760
Sorry. I think I need
to log out for today.

00:10:55.760 --> 00:10:57.930
Really? Now of all times?

00:10:57.930 --> 00:11:00.100
I have school tomorrow!

00:11:00.100 --> 00:11:04.600
Who cares about school?
Just enjoy the present.

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:07.190
What kind of adult says that?!

00:11:07.190 --> 00:11:09.230
The life of a shut-in is a valid choice.

00:11:09.230 --> 00:11:12.360
Even so, I'd like to stop for now!

00:11:12.360 --> 00:11:14.780
Okay, fine.

00:11:14.780 --> 00:11:16.990
Go ahead and save in case.

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:22.790
Huh? The save screen won't pop up...

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:26.750
KQ doesn't let you log out during combat.

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:28.000
So then...

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:31.130
You're not out of combat yet!

00:11:35.260 --> 00:11:38.550
There you are!

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:46.440
Ow!

00:11:46.440 --> 00:11:50.940
Stay calm! Pain is set to
be lower than in real life.

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:53.530
It doesn't feel like that to me!

00:11:53.530 --> 00:11:55.190
Even if you got a limb torn off,

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:59.410
it shouldn't hurt any more than full-body
bruises from falling down the stairs.

00:11:59.410 --> 00:12:00.370
No need to worry!

00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:02.910
That's not reassuring!

00:12:02.910 --> 00:12:08.960
What the hell is with all this mumbling?

00:12:08.960 --> 00:12:11.500
I-It's all over!

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:16.300
My eye!

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:18.260
Take this! And this!

00:12:18.260 --> 00:12:20.340
--What's happening?
--And one of these!

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:21.970
Reona.

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:22.850
Dammit!

00:12:22.850 --> 00:12:24.890
Hiro, hurry! Run!

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:27.560
R-Right!

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:29.190
Dammit!

00:12:29.190 --> 00:12:30.520
Hiro!

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:34.610
No matter where you run,
I swear I'll find you and kill you!

00:12:34.610 --> 00:12:36.400
Your fate is to be chopped up

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:42.740
by Hell's Fruit Slicer: Alicia,
the Fruit Knife Wielder From Hell!

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:47.660
What the hell is wrong with this game?

00:12:57.670 --> 00:13:02.800
How long has it been
since I ran all-out like that?

00:13:06.390 --> 00:13:07.720
Reona

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:07.850
Reona

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:14.570
Reona?

00:13:14.570 --> 00:13:16.820
Let's play KQ again today!

00:13:16.820 --> 00:13:18.280
When does school end?

00:13:18.280 --> 00:13:20.610
I'll log in, so make sure to join me!

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:23.370
Even if it kills you!

00:13:23.370 --> 00:13:25.950
Is this a threat?

00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:31.250
So did you get your new game?

00:13:31.250 --> 00:13:35.210
Actually, I was tricked into
getting this weird full-dive RPG.

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:36.960
Wait, what?

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:40.090
It's crazy realistic. You even feel pain.

00:13:40.090 --> 00:13:42.180
It's a game, but it hurts like crazy.

00:13:42.180 --> 00:13:43.970
So it's a shitty game?

00:13:43.970 --> 00:13:45.680
You got that right.

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:50.770
I'm sorry about yesterday.

00:13:50.770 --> 00:13:52.900
Video games are your hobby,

00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:55.020
and I didn't have any business
saying anything about it.

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:57.020
It's okay. I'm not mad or anything.

00:13:57.020 --> 00:13:58.820
Good.

00:13:58.820 --> 00:14:03.530
Though I do think it's
out of fashion and juvenile.

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:08.540
But for real, Hiro. You really need
to set them straight once and for all.

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:10.250
Look. Doesn't this rule?

00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:12.040
Ooh, sweet! Let's buy it.

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:14.670
We have our awesome friend, after all.

00:14:14.670 --> 00:14:16.540
You got that right!

00:14:18.300 --> 00:14:20.800
Th-They're not really a big--

00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:26.260
If you only ever play games,
you won't be treated with respect.

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:29.180
That may be true...

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:35.440
Out of fashion and juvenile...

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:38.610
And never treated with respect, huh?

00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:50.330
Kaede...

00:14:50.330 --> 00:14:51.700
I knew it.

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:52.830
Playing games again?

00:14:52.830 --> 00:14:54.580
Oh, no. I'm--

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:56.920
It's loud and annoying. For real.

00:14:56.920 --> 00:14:57.750
Huh?

00:14:57.750 --> 00:15:00.800
You were shouting and
screaming last night, too.

00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:05.880
Sorry. But it's okay. I was just
playing a game. No need to worry.

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:08.850
Who would worry about <i>you</i>?

00:15:08.850 --> 00:15:11.350
I wish you'd get rid of that crap.

00:15:11.350 --> 00:15:14.770
I-It's not some big problem
for me to have a hobby.

00:15:14.770 --> 00:15:18.110
If you're gonna have one, why not
take up running like you used to?

